    topics: [{ goal: "worship" }, { occasion: "day.patron-offering" }, { goal: "news" }],
    evidence: "documented",
    title: "Tsodilo, the great god and the lesser",
    text: "San religion speaks of a great god in the east who created the world and a lesser, trickster god in the west, who brings illness and death through the spirits of the dead. There were no temples or regular offerings; people spoke to the gods directly, sometimes angrily, and the chief rite was the healing dance, when women clapped and sang while men danced until some entered trance and drew sickness out of others. The Tsodilo Hills were a sacred place, and their thousands of paintings, made by San and later peoples, mark it as a place of the gods. News moved between bands by visiting: long trips to see kin were a way of learning where there was water, game and trouble.",
